From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:39:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt8781-zinwa-q25: Supply UFS VCC from
 VEMC

The UFS device's VCC comes from the MT6366 VEMC LDO, as in MediaTek's
board files. Without a consumer the regulator core switches VEMC off as
unused and the root filesystem disappears. With mediatek,ufs-broken-vcc
in the SoC dtsi the UFS driver keeps VCC always on.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
index ec02b3c4..1488c371 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
@@ -1317,6 +1317,7 @@
 };
 
 &ufs {
+	vcc-supply = <&mt6366_vemc_reg>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
